  "body": "### Summary\nAs a user, I want the offline-save banner's ✕ to have a 44 pt hit region, so that I can close the banner without aiming at a 16 pt glyph.\n\n### Scope\n- `App/SwiftHFR/Offline/ReaderOfflineSave.swift:87`: `Button(\"Fermer\", systemImage: \"xmark\").labelStyle(.iconOnly)` in an `HStack`, outside any List or toolbar. Its default style acts as a borderless button with no frame, so the hit region is the glyph alone (about 15 to 17 pt at `.body`).\n- Fix: the shared `.minimumHitRegion()` (#1292), keeping the look, with the overhang technique if the frame would move layout. Add a hosted frame test as in `ComposerTouchTargetTests` / `GifSearchClearTouchTargetTests`.\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] Hit region ≥ 44 × 44 pt at every Dynamic Type size, look unchanged, and the region does not cover the banner's text.\n- [ ] The test fails before the fix.\n\nFound by the adversarial review of #1328 (Opus 5.5, r1328), finding 3; spotted by w1296.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_\n",
